The attached image is Figure 7D from the PDF, a Western blot demonstrating that Nano-11 induces the secretion of the active 17 kD form of IL-1β. This figure provides crucial context to the ELISA results in Figure 7C. The blot shows that while LPS or Nano-11 alone primarily results in pro-IL-1β (30kD) in cell lysates, their combination significantly induces the cleavage and secretion of active IL-1β (17 kD band) into the supernatant. This confirms that Nano-11 activates caspase-1, leading to the processing and release of this potent pro-inflammatory cytokine, which is essential for its adjuvant effect on dendritic cells.